# 001 · Plans in public docs

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

Move the maintainers' private plans into `docs/plan/`: a roadmap, the v0.1.0 release plan, the settled decisions, and one goal for each roadmap item. Then archive the private plan files.

## Why

The plans had spread over many private files with five separate ID series. One public system is easier to follow, and testers can see what comes next.

## Done when

- [x] `docs/plan/` holds the roadmap, the release plan, the decisions and one goal for each roadmap item.
- [x] AGENTS.md, CONVENTIONS.md, the README and the docs index point to `docs/plan/`.
- [x] The public-content check passes on every file.
- [x] After the new plans reach the development branch, the old private plan files are archived, and new ideas arrive only as goals.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: The plans move to public docs. A new idea becomes a new goal and goes into the roadmap by priority. Plans hold no secrets and no details of a particular deployment.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-19: The plan files and the goals are written on a side branch. The cut-over waits until that branch merges.
- 2026-10-20: The plans reached the development branch. `docs/plan/` holds the roadmap, the release plan, the decisions and a goal for each roadmap item; AGENTS.md, CONVENTIONS.md, the README and the docs index point to it; the public check passes. The maintainers archived their private plan files, and new ideas now arrive only as goals. Verified.

---

Run with `/goal Complete docs/plan/goals/_completed/001-plans-in-public.goal`. Follow the [rules for every goal](../../README.md#rules-for-every-goal).
